  "Question": "Which of the following fractions has the largest value?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{7}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{4}{9}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{17}{35}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{100}{201}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{151}{301}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Comparing each fraction with \\(\\frac12\\) avoids finding a large common denominator. For a positive denominator, a fraction is below \\(\\frac12\\) when twice its numerator is smaller than its denominator.\n\nFor the first four choices, the doubled numerators satisfy \\(6<7\\), \\(8<9\\), \\(34<35\\), and \\(200<201\\). Thus all four fractions are less than \\(\\frac12\\).\n\nFor the last choice,\n\\[2\\cdot151=302>301,\\]\nso \\(\\frac{151}{301}>\\frac12\\). It is therefore larger than every other choice. The answer is \\(\\frac{151}{301}\\), choice E.",
